{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-36c64c59078bff41e301002b13df54e98f98c00b41b7fd6e","family_id":"KR:013220","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON MANAGEMENT OF FIREFIGHTING EQUIPMENT","title_original":"소방장비관리법 시행령","kind":"대통령령","source_version":"287377","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=287377","source_sha256":"5ec8ed6d9986beb9b06e27df3fdfd117ffbb23733f907e5568d570449f38d7fc","body_sha256":"570f44c93441ade91fb2764381e4a890b62439e019fbd3d195e14b192db8b07d","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 35 (Establishment of Cooperative Operational System of Firefighting Rotary-Wing Aircraft) (1) “Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree such as joint use of a control system” in Article 32 (1) of the Act means the following:\n  1. Joint use of a control system, etc. for real-time location information and flight information, etc. of firefighting rotary-wing aircraft;\n  2. Integrated management of maintenance quality such as maintenance standards and procedures, etc. for maintaining airworthiness of firefighting rotary-wing aircraft;\n  3. Improvement of the operating rate of firefighting rotary-wing aircraft through mutual support of maintenance personnel, facilities, equipment, parts, etc.;\n  4. Enhancement of Aviation safety for the prevention of accidents involving firefighting rotary-wing aircraft.\n  (2) Details of cooperation in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be determined by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency.","metadata":{"author_checks":["All current held source unit text, source editorial notes, amounts, periods, exceptions and source omission boundaries compared.","Unchanged official English retained only in the recorded exact source/target spans; original row, role, provider, edition, links and receipts remain unchanged.","New affected units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION / UNREVIEWED